WEBVTT

00:03.504 --> 00:06.440
Imperial Calendar Year 955

00:06.440 --> 00:11.111
As a result of the battle triggered
by the Triple Alliance's invasion...

00:11.111 --> 00:17.311
...the Humankind Abh Empire
began a huge retaliation.

00:17.818 --> 00:21.755
This retaliation was known as
Operation Phantom Flame.

00:21.755 --> 00:25.359
The Star Forces fleet of
Operation Phantom Flame...

00:25.359 --> 00:31.821
...has established a stronghold
in the enemy's territory.

00:32.633 --> 00:33.701
However, in response to
the Alliance's attack...

00:33.701 --> 00:36.704
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
However, in response to
the Alliance's attack...

00:36.704 --> 00:40.307
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
Operation Phantom Flame
has entered a new phase...

00:40.307 --> 00:41.075
...in which the objective is
to eliminate the enemy fleet.

00:41.075 --> 00:43.677
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...in which the objective is
to eliminate the enemy fleet.

00:43.677 --> 00:45.379
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
They await the Triple Alliance
in the Aptic System...

00:45.379 --> 00:46.013
They await the Triple Alliance
in the Aptic System...

00:46.013 --> 00:50.417
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...soon to be the main battlefield.

00:50.417 --> 00:50.651
...soon to be the main battlefield.

00:50.651 --> 00:51.085
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:51.085 --> 00:55.222
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:55.222 --> 00:55.956
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:55.956 --> 00:56.223
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:56.223 --> 00:56.924
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef

00:56.924 --> 01:00.327
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...Admiral Bebaus's defense
consists of only twelve squadrons.

01:00.327 --> 01:00.928
...Admiral Bebaus's defense
consists of only twelve squadrons.

01:00.928 --> 01:03.597
Aptic Defense Fleet Commander
Admiral Bebaus
...Admiral Bebaus's defense
consists of only twelve squadrons.

01:03.597 --> 01:04.398
Aptic Defense Fleet Commander
Admiral Bebaus
Given that they are outnumbered
by almost fifteen-to-one...

01:04.398 --> 01:09.670
Given that they are outnumbered
by almost fifteen-to-one...

01:09.670 --> 01:13.606
...the two fleets have decided on
the time of the decisive battle.

01:16.910 --> 01:18.579
Close the hatches!

01:18.579 --> 01:20.513
Hatches closed!

01:20.848 --> 01:22.182
Prepare to separate gangways...

01:22.182 --> 01:23.984
...and to store them away!

01:23.984 --> 01:24.952
Preparations complete!

01:24.952 --> 01:26.420
Commencing power!

01:26.420 --> 01:28.222
Separate gangways!

01:28.222 --> 01:29.390
Ignite engines!

01:29.390 --> 01:32.459
Engage the forward
stabilizers with pulse drive!

01:32.459 --> 01:33.961
All engines fully operational.

01:33.961 --> 01:35.729
Ready for departure!

01:35.729 --> 01:37.097
The stabilizers are ready to go.

01:37.097 --> 01:38.394
Ignite the main engine!

01:42.236 --> 01:43.103
I repeat.

01:43.103 --> 01:45.906
The enemy fleet is expected
to enter range within six hours.

01:45.906 --> 01:47.608
All ships depart.

01:47.608 --> 01:48.442
I repeat.

01:48.442 --> 01:51.211
The enemy fleet is expected
to enter combat within six hours.

01:51.211 --> 01:53.236
All ships depart.

02:08.262 --> 02:10.597
All engines are fully operational.

02:10.597 --> 02:13.167
Internal environment,
status normal.

02:13.167 --> 02:14.998
Ready for departure.

02:15.536 --> 02:17.527
Separate the gangway.

02:17.971 --> 02:20.132
Separating the gangway.

02:26.847 --> 02:28.248
Ignite the main engine!

02:28.248 --> 02:30.079
Igniting the main engine.

02:34.354 --> 02:35.753
Daisiele!

02:44.398 --> 02:48.061
The Basroil's Battle

02:53.640 --> 02:58.475
Banner of the Stars

04:17.357 --> 04:19.917
I've thought about this a little.

04:20.994 --> 04:22.029
No.

04:22.029 --> 04:26.728
It's got nothing to do with the Bebaus
brothers' relationship with you.

04:27.167 --> 04:28.869
I suppose that's a relief.

04:28.869 --> 04:30.200
So, what is this all about?

04:31.004 --> 04:34.872
How about we reinforce the
First Fleet a little more?

04:35.275 --> 04:36.674
The First Fleet?

04:37.611 --> 04:41.582
You mean have more patrol ships
than we had the last time?

04:41.582 --> 04:42.674
Yes.

04:43.150 --> 04:47.644
I think we can get hold of
twelve more squadrons.

04:47.854 --> 04:49.981
Maybe even as many as thirteen.

04:51.625 --> 04:53.422
Looks like I miscalculated!

04:55.629 --> 04:58.530
I take it you've already
considered this option?

04:59.032 --> 05:00.934
I didn't work it out.

05:00.934 --> 05:02.367
But the staff did.

05:03.270 --> 05:05.105
The enemy's formation
and strategy...

05:05.105 --> 05:07.374
...and the many other
uncertain factors...

05:07.374 --> 05:09.843
...made it difficult to predict
the correct course of action.

05:09.843 --> 05:10.777
In other words...

05:10.777 --> 05:13.614
...we can't be sure that increasing
the number of patrol ships...

05:13.614 --> 05:15.377
...will be the right decision.

05:16.316 --> 05:19.086
But if I go ahead and order the
strengthening of the First Fleet...

05:19.086 --> 05:20.954
...you won't object?

05:20.954 --> 05:21.784
No, I won't.

05:22.289 --> 05:22.889
However...

05:22.889 --> 05:25.525
...if that's the course of action
you're intending to take...

05:25.525 --> 05:27.427
...I've got one piece of
advice for you.

05:27.427 --> 05:28.451
And what's that?

05:28.895 --> 05:31.591
We should replace the
commander-in-chief.

05:34.801 --> 05:36.564
What's wrong with Beneej?

05:38.739 --> 05:41.775
With all these extra patrol ships...

05:41.775 --> 05:42.342
...she would be in charge of
twenty-five squadrons.

05:42.342 --> 05:43.944
Dalmap System
...she would be in charge of
twenty-five squadrons.

05:43.944 --> 05:46.380
Dalmap System
And that doesn't include
the supply ships.

05:46.380 --> 05:47.414
Dalmap System
I'm not concerned about...

05:47.414 --> 05:49.683
...Admiral Spoor's ability
to command...

05:49.683 --> 05:51.318
...but this is not appropriate
for her rank.

05:51.318 --> 05:53.754
Surely someone with a
higher rank should...

05:53.754 --> 05:55.522
If you're not concerned
about her ability...

05:55.522 --> 05:57.991
...let's leave it as is.

05:57.991 --> 06:00.994
I appreciate your point of view.

06:00.994 --> 06:05.465
But the First Fleet right now
has very few suited to command.

06:05.465 --> 06:07.134
Whether it's twelve or twenty-five...

06:07.134 --> 06:09.159
...it doesn't really matter.

06:10.470 --> 06:11.437
Your Highness...

06:12.272 --> 06:13.102
What is it now?

06:13.473 --> 06:16.143
Considering that you
backed Admiral Bebaus...

06:16.143 --> 06:19.046
...and that you support
Admiral Spoor...

06:19.046 --> 06:23.949
...are you giving those with
the blue blood special treatment?

06:25.686 --> 06:28.314
You should know what
you can say and what you can't.

06:28.855 --> 06:33.383
Even if I did have overconfident
expectations for them.

06:33.593 --> 06:34.494
Besides...

06:34.494 --> 06:37.597
...do you think I'd have the head
of the Spoors be assigned to...

06:37.597 --> 06:39.326
...a job that she's not suited to?

06:42.269 --> 06:44.032
You do have a point.

06:46.606 --> 06:51.043
Do you now acknowledge that
my decisions are not so perverse?

06:51.511 --> 06:55.174
Having Beneej in charge
is the most rational choice.

06:55.382 --> 06:57.551
That's all there is to it.

06:57.551 --> 06:58.752
Moreover...

06:58.752 --> 07:00.454
...I'm counting on the fact...

07:00.454 --> 07:03.617
...that Beneej will not enjoy
carrying out her position.

07:05.058 --> 07:06.026
I see.

07:06.026 --> 07:07.027
Now that you understand...

07:07.027 --> 07:08.927
...go and get in touch
with Beneej for me.

07:09.029 --> 07:10.428
Understood.

07:14.067 --> 07:15.836
One minute to the
rendezvous location!

07:15.836 --> 07:17.003
Shut down the main engine!

07:17.003 --> 07:18.372
Shutting down engine!

07:18.372 --> 07:19.339
Engage the stabilizers!

07:19.339 --> 07:20.774
Stabilizers engaged!

07:20.774 --> 07:22.843
Thirty seconds to the
rendezvous point!

07:22.843 --> 07:23.741
Arriving at assigned location.

07:24.177 --> 07:25.007
Shut down the main engine!

07:25.145 --> 07:27.170
Shutting down main engine!

07:28.048 --> 07:29.345
Arriving at the rendezvous point.

07:29.850 --> 07:31.685
Leaving stabilizers engaged...

07:31.685 --> 07:33.448
...and shutting down
the main engine.

07:37.157 --> 07:39.593
All crew are free to step away
from their stations.

07:39.593 --> 07:41.395
I want everyone to keep
on schedule...

07:41.395 --> 07:43.530
...and take turns at
getting some rest.

07:43.530 --> 07:44.792
Yes, Ma'am!

07:55.976 --> 07:57.000
Captain?

07:58.412 --> 08:01.108
Can I get you a drink?

08:01.515 --> 08:03.142
Yes. I'd like that.

08:04.117 --> 08:05.752
But if you want to be
on your own...

08:05.752 --> 08:06.912
...just tell me.

08:07.154 --> 08:09.987
I don't want you to think
you can't get rid of me.

08:10.257 --> 08:11.725
If you want to stay here with me...

08:11.725 --> 08:13.283
...it doesn't bother me.

08:16.396 --> 08:19.024
Can I get an exterior image?

08:23.870 --> 08:27.101
As a kid, I never
would've imagined...

08:27.307 --> 08:30.868
...that I'd see a view like this
with my own eyes.

08:31.445 --> 08:33.504
I always knew I'd see this.

08:33.713 --> 08:37.751
It was decided before I was born
that I would join the Star Forces...

08:37.751 --> 08:40.549
...and that one day I would
go to battle.

08:41.054 --> 08:41.888
However...

08:41.888 --> 08:45.619
...I hadn't anticipated being
the captain of an assault ship.

08:46.226 --> 08:49.718
I wanted to wear the
uniform of an admiral.

08:49.930 --> 08:51.531
You've got a long road ahead.

08:51.531 --> 08:54.159
I'm sure you'll get the
opportunity in the future.

08:54.367 --> 08:55.425
I suppose.

08:56.670 --> 08:59.901
What did you want to grow up
to be when you were a kid?

09:01.741 --> 09:03.643
I was only ten...

09:03.643 --> 09:06.771
...when the Empire came
and took control of our planet.

09:07.414 --> 09:11.316
I was too young to know then
what I wanted to do.

09:11.518 --> 09:15.318
But I do know that I never imagined
I'd make it out to space.

09:16.823 --> 09:19.018
You must have had many choices.

09:19.526 --> 09:20.322
That's right.

09:20.494 --> 09:21.862
Even though...

09:21.862 --> 09:24.490
...I don't think there was
much to choose from.

09:25.465 --> 09:26.557
Oh, I remember.

09:27.234 --> 09:30.003
My mother, before she died,
was a mining engineer.

09:30.003 --> 09:31.732
So I wanted to be
a mining engineer.

09:31.938 --> 09:35.876
Even though I didn't know
what it was about.

09:35.876 --> 09:37.138
What kind of work is it?

09:37.744 --> 09:42.148
Well, I'm not going to be
a mining engineer...

09:42.148 --> 09:44.139
...so it doesn't really matter.

09:45.118 --> 09:46.853
I wonder what it's like...

09:46.853 --> 09:50.490
...not to know what you will be
in the future.

09:50.490 --> 09:52.014
It can be unsettling.

09:52.559 --> 09:57.230
Sometimes you have to do
a job you hate just to get by.

09:57.230 --> 10:00.563
And that dream job you wanted
might turn out to be boring.

10:01.201 --> 10:02.869
To be honest with you...

10:02.869 --> 10:06.236
...I didn't think much about
what I wanted when I was a kid.

10:06.439 --> 10:10.243
But when I heard that I was
going to be Abh nobility...

10:10.243 --> 10:11.938
...I know I felt relieved.

10:12.612 --> 10:14.414
Even though it wasn't my choice...

10:14.414 --> 10:16.678
...it was a path I could take.

10:17.751 --> 10:20.120
Then I must have it easy.

10:20.120 --> 10:22.088
Whether I like it or not...

10:22.088 --> 10:24.190
...I've got to strive to be Empress.

10:24.190 --> 10:27.682
Do you really want to
become Empress?

10:28.094 --> 10:29.863
It's not that I want to be.

10:29.863 --> 10:33.233
Rather, I wanted to work
on a merchant ship.

10:33.233 --> 10:35.468
However, as an Abriel...

10:35.468 --> 10:38.960
...I have no choice but to take
my place on the imperial throne.

10:39.539 --> 10:42.337
Maybe I could go off and take a
real job, once I've done my duty.

10:43.109 --> 10:45.045
The family business, huh?

10:45.045 --> 10:49.311
Sometimes it seems the way
you people live is so simple.

10:50.016 --> 10:51.779
Don't forget you're an Abh, too.

10:52.485 --> 10:54.350
Yes, Lafiel, of course I know that.

10:55.989 --> 10:57.691
If this operation succeeds...

10:57.691 --> 11:02.355
...maybe the Hyde System will be
recaptured by the Empire.

11:02.696 --> 11:05.722
What will you do once
your territories are restored?

11:06.967 --> 11:08.059
Who knows?

11:08.835 --> 11:10.003
To be honest...

11:10.003 --> 11:12.405
...it'd be hard to go back
and see those people again.

11:12.405 --> 11:13.406
If possible...

11:13.406 --> 11:16.432
...I'd even trade places
with someone.

11:16.710 --> 11:18.511
You could always hire a deputy.

11:18.511 --> 11:19.739
I know.

11:20.280 --> 11:22.382
But it would feel like I'm
running away.

11:22.382 --> 11:23.849
And I wouldn't have a good excuse.

11:24.284 --> 11:25.919
You're working for the Star Forces.

11:25.919 --> 11:27.754
Isn't that a good enough reason?

11:27.754 --> 11:29.187
I suppose.

11:29.623 --> 11:31.358
After another ten years...

11:31.358 --> 11:34.191
...maybe I'll be disqualified
as a count.

11:35.662 --> 11:36.560
I've got an idea!

11:37.097 --> 11:38.826
Why don't we switch titles?!

11:39.165 --> 11:41.534
You can be Countess Hyde...

11:41.534 --> 11:44.697
...and I'll be Viscount Paryunu.
I could raise roses somewhere.

11:45.939 --> 11:48.134
There's no way we could do that.

11:48.808 --> 11:49.706
I suppose.

11:50.577 --> 11:53.137
Seemed like a good idea.

11:53.380 --> 11:54.314
Well...

11:54.314 --> 11:57.651
...I might've ended up being
called "Viscount of the Roses".

11:57.651 --> 11:59.719
Probably doesn't suit me.

11:59.719 --> 12:01.187
Forget it.

12:01.187 --> 12:02.518
Being a count is a duty.

12:03.056 --> 12:05.091
It's a duty I'd happily give away...

12:05.091 --> 12:07.293
...if there was someone
who wanted it.

12:07.293 --> 12:10.163
The noble title of Count Hyde
belongs to your family.

12:10.163 --> 12:11.798
It's not possible to give it away.

12:11.798 --> 12:12.696
Good grief.

12:12.899 --> 12:14.594
Like it haunts me.

12:15.135 --> 12:18.536
However, I'm the only
member of the Lin family.

12:18.738 --> 12:21.229
If I had a cousin somewhere,
I'd force the title on him.

12:22.242 --> 12:25.512
You should stay in the Star Forces
or work on a merchant ship.

12:25.512 --> 12:29.312
Lots of nobles who don't want
their territory end up doing that.

12:29.549 --> 12:30.447
Really?

12:30.884 --> 12:32.010
Maybe that's what I'll do.

12:32.352 --> 12:36.812
But I don't want the people back
home to think I'm chickening out.

12:38.425 --> 12:41.019
There are pros and cons
to everything.

12:41.227 --> 12:42.929
It's up to you to decide.

12:42.929 --> 12:45.090
Thanks for the helpful advice.

12:45.565 --> 12:49.669
I thought my life was decided
now that I'm an Abh noble.

12:49.669 --> 12:52.433
But it's nice to know
you can have fun, too.

12:52.806 --> 12:55.775
Even nobility needs to have fun.

12:55.775 --> 12:57.210
We, as Abh...

12:57.210 --> 13:00.179
...have three stages of life that we go
through before becoming an adult.

13:00.380 --> 13:02.082
You and I...

13:02.082 --> 13:05.518
...have only just started to
experience the first stage.

13:05.719 --> 13:09.086
Why worry about the future?
You can't do anything about it.

13:09.656 --> 13:13.319
But I don't spend much time
worrying about it.

13:13.526 --> 13:15.295
In any case...

13:15.295 --> 13:17.464
...what are these three stages of life?

13:17.464 --> 13:19.159
I think I know what
two of them are.

13:19.399 --> 13:21.167
One as an officer.

13:21.167 --> 13:23.369
And the other as a merchant.

13:23.369 --> 13:24.734
But what's the third?

13:25.338 --> 13:26.362
Don't you know?

13:26.740 --> 13:28.435
No. I don't.

13:28.875 --> 13:31.177
It's the most important stage
of the three.

13:31.177 --> 13:32.769
So, tell me what it is.

13:33.613 --> 13:34.978
When you become a parent.

13:38.118 --> 13:39.915
Hello, Beneej!

13:40.120 --> 13:42.055
Changed your hairstyle?

13:42.055 --> 13:42.953
No.

13:43.389 --> 13:46.950
I was about to go to sleep,
Your Highness.

13:47.327 --> 13:50.396
I apologize for the inconvenience.

13:50.396 --> 13:54.167
No matter what time of the day
or night it happens to be...

13:54.167 --> 13:56.101
...it's my greatest pleasure to
hear from Your Highness.

13:56.836 --> 13:58.599
What can I do for you?

14:04.110 --> 14:05.512
I see.

14:05.512 --> 14:09.516
So, our fleet may be engaged
in head-to-head combat...

14:09.516 --> 14:12.610
...with the enemy's elite
squadron of patrol ships?

14:13.286 --> 14:15.288
There is that possibility.

14:15.288 --> 14:18.324
I thought the plan was
for my dear fleet...

14:18.324 --> 14:22.090
...to deal a finishing blow to an
already tattered enemy in disarray.

14:22.796 --> 14:24.497
Whether your wish comes true...

14:24.497 --> 14:26.488
...depends on how the
enemy comes at us.

14:27.033 --> 14:29.936
Squadrons of patrol ships
fighting head-to-head...

14:29.936 --> 14:32.234
...seems rather brutish
and barbaric.

14:32.639 --> 14:36.131
There must be a way
headquarters can avoid this.

14:36.409 --> 14:37.967
We'll try to do our best.

14:38.344 --> 14:39.145
However...

14:39.145 --> 14:42.215
...I choose to win fighting
like a barbarian...

14:42.215 --> 14:45.548
...than to lose elegantly.

14:45.752 --> 14:49.916
You're giving me a task that's
more suited to an Abriel.

14:52.559 --> 14:55.662
You're a very unkind man.

14:55.662 --> 14:56.526
Good night.

14:57.330 --> 15:01.301
Beneej said that I was unkind.

15:01.301 --> 15:04.270
Should I be taking it
as a compliment?

15:04.504 --> 15:06.597
Please don't ask me.

15:10.977 --> 15:14.743
Every time I talk to His Highness,
it throws me off.

15:16.015 --> 15:19.185
I know Abriels are famous
for being terribly serious.

15:19.185 --> 15:23.122
But that man just
doesn't take the bait.

15:23.122 --> 15:26.148
It's no fun teasing him.

15:26.526 --> 15:28.061
Perhaps that's because...

15:28.061 --> 15:33.466
...being teased by you is not
why the royal family exists.

15:33.466 --> 15:35.235
Well, my dear Chief of Staff...

15:35.235 --> 15:38.136
...I've never looked at things that way.

15:39.205 --> 15:40.373
Preparations to fire...

15:40.373 --> 15:43.069
...space-time mines from the front
line battle ships are complete.

15:43.843 --> 15:47.080
All ships working near the front
line ships must now clear the area.

15:47.080 --> 15:47.814
I repeat!

15:47.814 --> 15:51.580
All ships working near the front
line ships must now clear the area.

15:55.488 --> 15:56.456
Front line ships...

15:56.456 --> 15:58.583
...launch space-time mines!

15:58.925 --> 16:00.950
Space-time mines launched!

16:01.661 --> 16:03.356
Space-time mines launched!

16:05.531 --> 16:08.466
Space-time mines ready to be
positioned for detonation.

16:09.302 --> 16:10.769
The battle is about to begin.

16:11.137 --> 16:13.806
I need you to relay an
urgent message to all units!

16:13.806 --> 16:17.277
All crew are to take up
battle positions immediately!

16:17.277 --> 16:17.766
Roger!

16:19.012 --> 16:20.713
Assault Vessel
Latouche Contingent!

16:20.713 --> 16:22.482
All ships to take up
battle positions!

16:22.482 --> 16:23.683
I repeat!

16:23.683 --> 16:25.585
Assault Vessel
Latouche Contingent!

16:25.585 --> 16:27.654
All ships to take up
battle positions!

16:27.654 --> 16:30.223
Assault Vessel
Burushusyunraafu Contingent!

16:30.223 --> 16:32.725
All ships to take up
battle positions!

16:32.725 --> 16:33.593
I repeat!

16:33.593 --> 16:36.229
Assault Vessel
Burushusyunraafu Contingent!

16:36.229 --> 16:38.398
All ships to take up
battle positions!

16:38.398 --> 16:39.299
I repeat!

16:39.299 --> 16:40.900
Assault Vessel
Aruroo Contingent!

16:40.900 --> 16:42.697
All ships to take up
battle positions!

16:43.202 --> 16:45.471
Assault Vessel
Kookusyundoo Contingent!

16:45.471 --> 16:47.371
All ships to take up
battle positions!

16:48.174 --> 16:49.842
All ships are now in position!

16:49.842 --> 16:53.744
Enemy fleet estimated
to arrive in thirty minutes.

16:54.447 --> 16:56.540
So, our main fleet is over here...

16:58.151 --> 17:01.487
If we wait for them, they might
arrive in fifty hours or so.

17:01.487 --> 17:03.887
The enemy must know that, too.

17:04.691 --> 17:06.386
They'll come at us with
all they've got.

17:06.693 --> 17:08.854
I wouldn't have it any other way.

17:09.662 --> 17:11.297
This war isn't happening...

17:11.297 --> 17:13.026
...just for your entertainment.

17:13.166 --> 17:16.226
I don't mean that we should
have fun from war.

17:16.602 --> 17:20.440
If it turns out to be fun,
then what can you say?

17:20.440 --> 17:21.372
Is that so?

17:21.741 --> 17:23.009
Of course.

17:23.009 --> 17:25.144
The lives of our crew
are at stake here.

17:25.144 --> 17:27.840
We're not going to alter strategy
for the sake of entertainment...

17:28.114 --> 17:31.140
...if that's what you're worried about.

17:31.684 --> 17:34.949
Actually, that's exactly
what I am worried about.

17:35.355 --> 17:37.721
I hope you won't forget
what you just said.

17:38.057 --> 17:41.857
We don't want our family's
reputation to sink any lower.

17:42.462 --> 17:43.496
No.

17:43.496 --> 17:46.397
Perhaps we should say
"get any higher"?!

17:46.599 --> 17:47.691
Don't worry.

17:47.967 --> 17:50.069
I personally have nothing
to do with...

17:50.069 --> 17:51.838
...the Bebaus family's notoriety.

17:51.838 --> 17:54.474
All that it takes to make me happy...

17:54.474 --> 17:56.442
...is to lead an ordinary life.

17:56.442 --> 17:58.144
So being an admiral...

17:58.144 --> 18:01.375
...and commanding a fleet
is your idea of an ordinary life?

18:01.881 --> 18:04.350
I think your attitude
has just proved...

18:04.350 --> 18:08.821
...that you suffer from our family's
affliction more than you realize.

18:08.821 --> 18:09.555
In that case...

18:09.555 --> 18:12.625
...stop spending so much time
making me worry about it.

18:12.625 --> 18:14.961
Otherwise I might get the urge...

18:14.961 --> 18:18.197
...to add yet another chapter to the
history of our Spectacular Insanity.

18:18.197 --> 18:19.499
Don't worry.

18:19.499 --> 18:21.267
I'm going to be here with you.

18:21.267 --> 18:24.668
If it comes to it, I'll even kill you
in order to stop you.

18:25.338 --> 18:28.074
Now I'm even more worried,
Nefee.

18:28.074 --> 18:30.376
I don't have a problem with you
killing me...

18:30.376 --> 18:34.073
...but I'd like it to be for a reason
that anyone can understand.

18:34.747 --> 18:36.883
Transmission received
from the Koosururu!

18:36.883 --> 18:40.080
The enemy has launched
several space-time mines!

18:40.453 --> 18:43.790
Enemy makes the first move,
as we chat away idly.

18:43.790 --> 18:45.391
What's the time of arrival?

18:45.391 --> 18:46.858
About seven minutes!

18:47.326 --> 18:48.987
Should we counterattack?

18:49.562 --> 18:51.397
We don't have much choice.

18:51.397 --> 18:54.067
We can't let them tear us apart
without some retaliation.

18:54.067 --> 18:56.536
You're making good sense, Nereis.

18:56.536 --> 18:58.128
Thank you very much.

18:58.938 --> 19:01.338
Fire all mines directly
into the Sord!

19:01.474 --> 19:03.669
Issue this order to the fleet!

19:17.156 --> 19:18.748
So, it has begun.

19:55.661 --> 19:58.824
All mines have now
entered the Sord!

19:58.965 --> 20:02.025
It makes you feel defenseless.

20:02.401 --> 20:03.402
No.

20:03.402 --> 20:05.029
We've been defenseless
from the start.

20:05.538 --> 20:08.174
Whether there're mines
ahead of us or not...

20:08.174 --> 20:11.007
...the armor of an assault ship
is very thin.

20:12.345 --> 20:14.780
It's going to be impossible
for us to destroy...

20:14.780 --> 20:16.182
...every one of those
enemy mines.

20:16.182 --> 20:19.481
And there's no doubt
some of them are headed our way.

20:20.186 --> 20:21.320
Stay calm.

20:21.320 --> 20:24.778
You have the fate of twenty lives
in your hands.

20:25.925 --> 20:29.554
An officer of the Star Forces
has a responsibility to his crew.

20:30.329 --> 20:31.631
Senior Aviator...

20:31.631 --> 20:34.657
...do you remember the mines
that misfired in Wimpel?

20:35.334 --> 20:37.894
I was thinking the same thing.

20:46.445 --> 20:47.878
What are you worried about?

20:48.014 --> 20:49.115
Back then...

20:49.115 --> 20:51.140
...we thought we had destroyed
all the mines.

20:51.651 --> 20:52.117
That's right.

20:52.451 --> 20:53.519
However...

20:53.519 --> 20:56.422
...we then realized what was in
those two space-time bubbles.

20:56.422 --> 20:59.058
There were seven mines
hidden in there.

20:59.058 --> 20:59.825
The enemy's...

20:59.825 --> 21:01.224
...new weapon?

21:03.729 --> 21:05.097
The enemy mines at the head...

21:05.097 --> 21:06.564
...are due to arrive at any second!

21:07.166 --> 21:08.827
Mines directly in front of us!

21:14.207 --> 21:16.008
I don't know what it is, but...

21:16.008 --> 21:17.143
Second Aviator!

21:17.143 --> 21:19.278
It may be debris,
but keep a close eye on it!

21:19.278 --> 21:20.006
Roger!

21:20.446 --> 21:21.344
Are we ready to go?

21:21.547 --> 21:22.648
Line Wing Aviator?

21:22.648 --> 21:23.416
Yes.

21:23.416 --> 21:26.519
Can't you feel the air in here
bubbling with excitement?!

21:26.519 --> 21:29.317
We can move at any time now
with maximum speed!

21:29.555 --> 21:30.112
Good.

21:32.024 --> 21:33.321
Let the battle commence!

21:38.598 --> 21:40.964
First on the scene is the Basroil...

21:41.500 --> 21:44.070
They sure have a lot of enthusiasm.

21:44.070 --> 21:45.833
Is that the blood of the Abriel?

21:46.572 --> 21:48.341
I'm sorry, but...

21:48.341 --> 21:51.674
...I can't let Your Imperial Highness
take all the glory in this battle.

21:59.485 --> 22:01.248
Stay calm, Lafiel.

22:02.588 --> 22:04.522
Prepare to fire the
anti-proton cannon!

22:04.991 --> 22:07.721
Preparations to fire the
anti-proton cannon complete!

22:09.762 --> 22:11.229
The three stages of life...

22:12.064 --> 22:13.725
And I'm only at the first.

22:14.300 --> 22:15.901
Until I experience all three...

22:15.901 --> 22:17.266
...I'm not going to give up!

22:18.137 --> 22:21.197
The enemy mines will be
within range in ten seconds.

22:21.807 --> 22:25.378
Eight... seven... six... five...

22:25.378 --> 22:29.248
...four... three... two... one.

22:29.248 --> 22:30.977
Enemy mine is now within range!

22:36.055 --> 22:37.613
Fire the anti-proton cannon!

22:42.862 --> 22:47.900
Month of Roswik, Day 11, 14: 12
The Basroil's Battle Begins

22:47.900 --> 22:52.837
Arrival of the Main Fleet
50 hours to go...

22:54.240 --> 22:58.540
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.078 --> 23:03.344
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.583 --> 23:08.280
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.522 --> 23:13.322
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.592 --> 23:15.561
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.561 --> 23:19.554
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.766 --> 23:25.938
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:25.938 --> 23:29.669
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:29.909 --> 23:34.073
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.613 --> 23:38.984
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:38.984 --> 23:46.192
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.192 --> 23:51.464
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.464 --> 24:00.031
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.007 --> 24:07.146
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.146 --> 24:12.551
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.551 --> 24:20.925
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.193 --> 24:25.630
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:36.208 --> 24:37.573
Their new weapon?

24:39.512 --> 24:42.072
You're not fooling around,
are you?

24:50.489 --> 24:51.581
They are almost like...

24:55.961 --> 24:57.863
...the souls...

24:57.863 --> 25:00.832
Next Episode...
Shooting Star
